    "answer": {
      "short": "The fifth power of a whole number ends in the same digit as the original number.",
      "worked": "Experiment with each possible final digit:\n$$\\begin{align*}0^5&=0 &1^5&=1\\\\2^5&=32 &3^5&=243\\\\4^5&=1024 &5^5&=3125\\\\6^5&=7776 &7^5&=16807\\\\8^5&=32768 &9^5&=59049\\end{align*}$$\nIn every case, the final digit is unchanged. The final digit of a product depends only on its factors' final digits, so this pattern applies to any whole number.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
